-- src:313 | (Submission of Materials and Other Forms of Cooperation)
-- src:314 | Article 25 (1) If the headquarters finds it necessary for performing the affairs
-- src:315 | under their jurisdiction, they may request the heads of a relevant
-- src:316 | administrative body, local government, incorporated administrative agency
-- src:317 | (meaning the incorporated administrative agency prescribed in Article 2,
-- src:318 | paragraph (1) of Act on General Rules for Incorporated Administrative
-- src:319 | Agencies (Act No. 103 of 1999)) and local incorporated administrative agency
-- src:320 | (meaning the local incorporated administrative agency prescribed in Article 2,
-- src:321 | paragraph (1) of the Local Independent Administrative Agency Act (Act No.
-- src:322 | 118 of 2003)), and the representative of a special corporation (meaning the
-- src:323 | corporation directly incorporated by law or corporation incorporated by a
-- src:324 | special act of incorporation pursuant to a special law, to which the provisions
-- src:325 | of Article 4, paragraph (1), item (viii) of the Act for Establishment of the
-- src:326 | Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications (Act No. 91 of 1999) apply) to
-- src:327 | submit materials, express opinions, give explanations and provide other
-- src:328 | necessary cooperation.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:79 | （資料の提出その他の協力）
-- src:ai-act-ja:80 | 第二十五条 本部は、その所掌事務を遂行するため必要があると認めるときは、関係行政機関、地方公共団体、独立行政法人（独立行政法人通則法（平成十一年法律第百三号）第二条第一項に規定する独立行政法人をいう。）及び地方独立行政法人（地方独立行政法人法（平成十五年法律第百十八号）第二条第一項に規定する地方独立行政法人をいう。）の長並びに特殊法人（法律により直接に設立された法人又は特別の法律により特別の設立行為をもって設立された法人であって、総務省設置法（平成十一年法律第九十一号）第四条第一項第八号の規定の適用を受けるものをいう。）の代表者に対して、資料の提出、意見の表明、説明その他必要な協力を求めることができる。
--
-- The Headquarters may request cooperation from the heads of relevant administrative
-- bodies, local governments, incorporated administrative agencies and local
-- incorporated administrative agencies, and from the representatives of special
-- corporations. A special corporation (特殊法人) is defined by how it was set up, not
-- by what it does, so one that uses the technology in its business is a utilization
-- business operator too; that is why this row's bearing is not "none". The Act
-- states no duty to comply and no consequence.
@ref Article 25(1) (src:313-328) (src:ai-act-ja:79-80)
GIVETH A `A provision`
`Article 25(1)` MEANS
    `A provision` WITH
        `the provision`                         IS "Article 25(1)"
        `in the main provisions`                IS TRUE
        `the article number`                    IS 25
        `part`                                  IS `Chapter IV, Artificial Intelligence Strategic Headquarters`
        `addressed to`                          IS `the Headquarters or its officers (本部, 本部長, 副本部長, 本部員)`
        `the verb form`                         IS `may request (求めることができる)`
        `what it means for a business operator` IS `the Headquarters may request cooperation from the representative of a special corporation, which can itself be a business operator`
        `mechanisms affecting a private person` IS EMPTY

-- src:329 | (2) If the headquarters finds it particularly necessary for performing the affairs
-- src:330 | under their jurisdiction, they may ask for necessary cooperation from a person
-- src:331 | other than those prescribed in the preceding paragraph.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:81 | ２ 本部は、その所掌事務を遂行するために特に必要があると認めるときは、前項に規定する者以外の者に対しても、必要な協力を依頼することができる。
--
-- "A person other than those prescribed in the preceding paragraph" reaches a private
-- business. 依頼することができる, "may ask for", is softer than paragraph (1)'s 求めることができる. The Act
-- states no duty to comply and no consequence; whether Article 7 makes cooperation a
-- duty is fork F5.
@ref Article 25(2) (src:329-331) (src:ai-act-ja:81)
